course: dictionary
lesson: 8899
title: Shrug and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A shrug is a small movement of the shoulders: you lift them quickly and let them drop. People shrug when they do not know the answer or do not care much. «His mate shrugs.» You can see the meaning from the action, even without words.
explain: Shrug can be a verb or a noun. You can shrug, shrugs, shrugged or shrugging, and a shrug is the movement itself: «With a shrug, she walked on.» When you meet it in a story, read the words around it to find the clues.
explain: Shrug also has a useful phrase, shrug it off. It means to treat something as not important, or to get over it easily. «Kieran shrugged it off and laughed.» Try your meaning in the sentence: does "he did not think it mattered" still make sense? If it does, you have it.
fact: To shrug is to raise your shoulders quickly and drop them.
fact: A shrug can show that you do not know something, or that you do not care.
fact: «Shrug your shoulders» and «shrug it off» are common phrases.
fact: «Shrug it off» means to treat something as not important.
fact: Shrug can be a verb («shrugged») or a noun («a shrug»).
exercise: «His mate shrugs.» What does the shrug show? | He is dancing | He is very tall | *He does not know, or does not care | He is angry and shouting
exercise: «Kieran shrugged it off and laughed.» What does shrug it off mean? | *Treat it as not important | Wrap it up tightly | Pick it up and carry it home | Shout at it loudly
exercise: «With a shrug, she walked on.» Find and copy the noun that is the movement. | she | on | walked | *shrug
test: «She gave a shrug and said, I don't mind.» What does the shrug show? | She is falling asleep | *She does not care much | She is cold and wet | She is very angry
test: «Dad shrugged his shoulders when we asked where the biscuits had gone.» What does shrugged mean here? | Ran off to find them | Jumped up and down | *Raised his shoulders and dropped them, showing he did not know | Closed his eyes tightly
exam: Which phrase means to treat a problem as not important? | *Shrug it off | Shrug the bag | Shout it out | Hide under a hat
